Subject: [PATCH] lmdb: Don't let a command-line CFLAGS override drop `-fPIC`

Backport of https://github.com/JuliaLang/julia/pull/63055 (as of cbdc35c42),
which is not merged yet. Drop this patch once it has landed in the pinned
master commit.

LMDB's Makefile defines `CFLAGS = $(THREADS) $(OPT) $(W) $(XCFLAGS)`, so
passing our flags via `XCFLAGS` only works as long as nothing overrides
`CFLAGS`. BinaryBuilder passes `CFLAGS=` on the top-level make command line,
which propagates into every sub-make through `MAKEOVERRIDES` and takes
precedence over LMDB's own definition, so `XCFLAGS` is never expanded and
`-fPIC` is silently dropped. `liblmdb.a` is statically linked into
libjulia-codegen, so the non-PIC objects then break that link on every
target whose toolchain does not default to PIE.

diff --git a/deps/lmdb.mk b/deps/lmdb.mk
index 290a2f600d2bc..3df44d09caa7a 100644
--- a/deps/lmdb.mk
+++ b/deps/lmdb.mk
@@ -11,6 +11,10 @@ LMDB_SRC_SUBDIR := libraries/liblmdb
 LMDB_BUILD_OPTS := CC="$(CC)" AR="$(AR)" prefix=$(abspath $(build_prefix))
 # -fPIC so the static archive can be linked into the libjulia-codegen shared library
 LMDB_BUILD_OPTS += XCFLAGS="$(CFLAGS) $(fPIC)"
+# we pass our flags to LMDB via XCFLAGS, but this only works as long as
+# nothing overrides CFLAGS; so restore the default LMDB CFLAGS here
+# (this is important for libjulia_jll)
+LMDB_BUILD_OPTS += CFLAGS='$$(THREADS) $$(OPT) $$(W) $$(XCFLAGS)'
 # Select LMDB's robust lock backend, including SysV semaphores on Apple/BSD.
 LMDB_BUILD_OPTS += CPPFLAGS="-DMDB_USE_ROBUST=1"
 
